            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- **Electrons** (negative charge) — orbit around the nucleus",
            "start": 411,
            "end": 471
          },
          {
            "id": "p11",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "The **number of protons** determines what element an atom is. For example, every carbon atom has exactly 6 protons — that's what makes it carbon!",
            "start": 473,
            "end": 618
          },
          {
            "id": "p12",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "However, the **number of neutrons can vary**, even for the same element. This variation creates isotopes.",
            "start": 620,
            "end": 725
          },
          {
            "id": "p13",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
